WEBVTT

00:31:28.811 --> 00:31:32.814
I'm just saying, you know, protect
the other side of human needs, as well.

00:31:32.838 --> 00:31:36.477
If you think of this
in terms of stimulation,

00:31:36.501 --> 00:31:39.450
for all of us, whether
we're introverts or extroverts,

00:31:39.474 --> 00:31:43.520
our craving for stimulation
fluctuates throughout the day.

00:31:43.544 --> 00:31:44.977
And so, you want people,

00:31:45.001 --> 00:31:47.785
when they're at the moment
where they need stimulation,

00:31:47.809 --> 00:31:50.383
you want them to have access
to a nice, social space.

00:31:50.407 --> 00:31:53.236
And then the moment
that they need to chill it out,

00:31:53.260 --> 00:31:55.587
you want them to have access
to that phone booth,

00:31:55.611 --> 00:31:58.841
because that's how they're going to
be most productive and happiest.

00:31:58.865 --> 00:32:05.197
I'm going to say also a bigger point
beyond office spaces, which is: